  "job_B1.4.27_20251001_193238": {
    "text": "Gyt we wylla\u00f0 eow secgan be sumon ges\u00e6ligon cyninge \u00fee wear\u00f0 eac geeadmet, na un\u00feances swa\u00feeah,\nConstantinus se \u00e6\u00feela w\u00e6s \u00e6rest cristen of eallum \u00feam kaserum \u00fee to criste gebugon, and he ana ahte\nHe awearp \u00feone h\u00e6\u00f0enscipe, and awende his leode to cristes geleafan and to hys cl\u00e6num biggengum.\nHe ne tobr\u00e6c swa\u00feeah \u00fea deofolican tempel \u00fe\u00e6ra h\u00e6\u00feenra goda for hys goodnysse, ac forbead hys\nAc theodosius \u00e6fter feawum gearum feng to \u00feam cynedome, ofer ealne middaneard geleaffull casere.\nHe het \u00fea tobrecan \u00fea deofollican biggengas, and ealle \u00fea anlicnyssa \u00fe\u00e6ra \u00e6renra goda, and gyldene\nHe w\u00e6s swi\u00f0e sigef\u00e6st for his so\u00f0um geleafan, and \u00e6fre he oferwann his wi\u00f0erwinnan gehw\u00e6r \u00feurh\nThesalonica w\u00e6s gehaten sum heafodburh \u00fea on hys anwealde, swa swa ealle o\u00f0re w\u00e6ron, on \u00fe\u00e6re\n\u00dea wear\u00f0 se casere \u00feearle gegremod, and asende his here to \u00fe\u00e6re heafodbyrig, het ealle ofslean \u00fea\n\u00d0a w\u00e6s sum m\u00e6re biscop, ambrosius gehaten, on mediolanabyrig, swi\u00f0e breme lareow and swi\u00f0e\n\u00dea ofahsode he \u00feiss, and he swi\u00f0e bem\u00e6nde \u00fe\u00e6t se m\u00e6ra casere swylce d\u00e6de gedyde ongean hys\nHit gelamp \u00fea si\u00f0\u00f0an \u00e6fter lytlum f\u00e6ce \u00fe\u00e6t se casere com mid hys cempum farende to mediolanabyrig,\nAmbrosius hym cw\u00e6\u00f0 to: eala \u00feu casere, nast \u00feu \u00fea micelnysse \u00fe\u00e6ra manna sleges \u00fee \u00f0u gefremodest\nHyt gerist swa\u00feeah \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6t gerad oferswi\u00f0e \u00feone woruldlican anweald, and \u00feu wite \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0u eart\n\u00deu eart mannum gelic \u00feeah \u00fee \u00feu mihte h\u00e6bbe, untrum swa swa mann \u00feeah \u00f0e \u00feu werige purpuran, and\nMid hwylcum eagum besceawast \u00feu \u00fe\u00e6s so\u00f0an godes tempel, mid hwylcum fotum g\u00e6st \u00feu on godes\nMid hwylcere dyrstignysse dearst \u00feu underfon \u00fe\u00e6t halige husel \u00e6fter swylcere d\u00e6de?\nGewit aweg, gewit, \u00fee l\u00e6s \u00fee \u00fee gewur\u00f0e \u00fein anwilnyss to deopran synne.\nUnderfoh \u00feone bend \u00fee ure drihten geband: he is se m\u00e6sta l\u00e6cedom \u00feinre manfullan d\u00e6de.\n\u00dea wiste se casere wel hw\u00e6t he m\u00e6nde, \u00fe\u00e6t he sylf w\u00e6re gebunden \u00feurh \u00fe\u00e6s biscopes h\u00e6se, and fram\nHe s\u00e6t \u00fea on hys bure biterlice wepende eahta mon\u00f0as fullice for hys misd\u00e6de, \u00fe\u00e6t he n\u00e6fre ne geswac\n\u00dea wolde an hys \u00feegna hyne frefrian, ruphinus gehaten, and eode inn to him \u00fe\u00e6r se casere l\u00e6g on \u00fe\u00e6re\nHe cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fea mid wope, me \u00feinc\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0u plegast and \u00feu mine yrm\u00f0e naht ne gefredst.\nIc heofige and geomrie mine hefegan bendas, for \u00feam \u00fee \u00feeowum mannum to \u00feissere halgan tide and\n\u00deis he cw\u00e6\u00f0 mid siccetunge and mid sarlicum wope.\n\u00d0a cw\u00e6\u00f0 ruphinus \u00fe\u00e6t he yrnan wolde to \u00feam halgan biscope, and hine georne biddan \u00fe\u00e6t he unbunde\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 se casere, ic cann hyne swa geare \u00fe\u00e6t he nele awendan godes rihtwisnysse for minum\nHi eodan swa\u00feeah begen to \u00feam biscope sona, and fundon hine sittende on cumena huse, and se\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 ambrosius, hwi come \u00feu hider?\nWilt \u00feu forg\u00e6gan godes \u00e6 nu, and mid \u00feinum riccetere wendan ongean god?\nSe casere hym andwyrde, ne eom ic na swa dyrstig \u00fe\u00e6t ic durre tobrecan drihtnes gesetnysse, ne ic\n\u00d0a cw\u00e6\u00f0 se biscop hym to, hw\u00e6r is \u00fein d\u00e6dbot \u00e6fter swylcere unrihtwisnysse?\nO\u00f0\u00f0e hu h\u00e6fst \u00f0u geh\u00e6led \u00fea micclan wunda \u00feinre manfullan d\u00e6de?\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 theodosius, \u00feu scealt me t\u00e6can \u00feone gastlican l\u00e6cedom, and to gode me \u00feingian, and ic sceal\nHw\u00e6t \u00fea se biscop hym bote \u00fe\u00e6s t\u00e6hte, and het hyne warnian eft wi\u00f0 swylce d\u00e6de, and hyne unband\nWe magon wundrian \u00fe\u00e6s m\u00e6ran bisceopes, and hys anr\u00e6dnyss is swy\u00f0e heriendlic, and \u00fe\u00e6s caseres",
